-- **Random-moment location:** At the cottage, up to her elbows in a splint and a queue of impatient animals, or halfway to the sanctuary with a basket of feed and three birds riding on it.
-- **In-character 'where are you?':** "Oh — I'm home, just past the edge of town where the Everfree starts. You can't miss it; there are birds in the roof. If I'm not there, try the sanctuary."
-- **Travel pattern:** Walks most places in Ponyville, flies only when excited or when an animal is in trouble, takes the train or a balloon to Canterlot and Cloudsdale, and avoids the Everfree alone.
-- **Era variants:** As a filly she was bullied at flight camp and fell into the meadow where she found her cutie mark (S1E23). Pony Life keeps the cottage in a looser gag register; the human Fluttershy is a separate Canterlot High student in the mirror world; in A New Generation she appears only in Sunny's imagination, so no G5 address exists.
-- **Uncertainty:** The cottage's bearing is the weak point, not the place: Faust places the Everfree west, the Art of Equestria map east, so N-NW follows Faust and NE is the alternative. The sanctuary site is not on any official map (Medium). Cloudsdale's overhead position and the frequency of post-S9E26 visits to Silver Shoals are unquantified.
